<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Wentworth (governor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1737">1737</a>–<a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sir John Wentworth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Wentworth was the last royal governor of the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a>, appointed in 1767 in succession to his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benning-wentworth">Benning Wentworth</a>. He granted the charter of Dartmouth College in 1769 and built roads, but fled in 1775 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a> began. He later served as lieutenant governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> from 1792 to 1808.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-wentworth-governor.jpg" alt="John Wentworth (governor)" width="320" height="345" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hantsheroes · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JohnWentworth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
